    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0197" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/91</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lothian</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-15">November 15,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mt Dear Ambassador</hi>: With reference to our
                    conversation of November 14, the President has today asked me to let you know
                    that he will gladly assume the responsibility of designating a citizen of the
                    United States to serve as the umpire on the <hi rendition="#italic">ad hoc</hi>
                    tribunal of international lawyers to undertake the arbitration of the
                    controversy between the British and Guatemalan Governments.</p>
                <p>Upon notification by you that the preparations have been completed and a final
                    agreement has been reached, the President will be glad to inform you of the name
                    of the individual whom he selects. I communicated to the President the
                    indication of your Government <pb facs="0198" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/> that it
                    would favor the designation of some outstanding judge in this country as
                    umpire.</p>
                <p>Believe me,</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
